% The Ponens policies jsf-av-cpp, as a program of Logical English for LPS.
%
% Written by lpsPlus's ponens_twin.pl (docs/migration/ponens.md) from 12
% Ponens policies, whose files are in sources/ (Ponens: github.com/imandra-ai/
% ponens, MIT licence), with 2 Ponens traces as its scenarios.
%
% Each step of a trace is an action of the session Ponens recorded. Each
% policy is a causal law that records a breach: at the step where the policy
% fails, when the step ends, or at the end of the session when the policy
% looks forward. Where a scenario has a comment above it, the comment is what
% Ponens's own evaluator (`ponens trace check --json`) says of the same
% policies on that trace.
%
% DISCLAIMER. This program was written by a translator from the policies of
% another system. It is provided "as is", without warranty of any kind,
% express or implied, including any warranty that it is accurate, complete or
% fit for a particular purpose. The translation may be wrong: check it against
% its source before relying on it. It is not legal, regulatory or other
% professional advice. Its authors accept no liability for any loss or damage
% arising from its use.

the target language is: lps.

the maximum time is 20.

the events are:
    step *a step* is a *a kind*; known as step_is_a.
    step *a step* shows *a sign*; known as step_shows.
    step *a step* ends; known as step_ends.
    the trace shows *a sign*; known as trace_shows.
    the session ends; known as session_ends.

the fluents are:
    step *a step* was a *a kind*; known as was_a.
    step *a step* has shown *a sign*; known as has_shown.
    step *a step* has ended; known as has_ended.
    the trace has shown *a sign*; known as trace_has_shown.
    step *a step* meets *a condition*; known as meets.
    the policy *a policy* is broken at step *a step*; known as broken_at.

the knowledge base jsf av cpp includes:

% What a trace records, kept to the end of the session.
when step a step is a a kind
then step the step was a the kind.

when step a step shows a sign
then step the step has shown the sign.

when step a step ends
then step the step has ended.

when the trace shows a sign
then the trace has shown the sign.

% jsf_certified_libraries_only (error): G(safety_critical ∧ library_use → certified_library)
% JSF++ AV Rule 16: only DO-178B Level A certifiable or SEAL 1 C/C++ libraries shall be used with safety-critical (SEAL 1) code.
when step a step ends
    and step the step has shown "safety critical"
    and step the step has shown "library use"
    and it is not the case that step the step has shown "certified library"
then the policy jsf_certified_libraries_only is broken at step the step.

% jsf_deviation_record_maintained (error): G(Deviation → rationale_recorded ∧ approval_recorded)
% JSF++ AV Rules 4-6: deviations are recorded with rationale and the approvals obtained (engineering lead, and product manager for shall/will rules).
step a step meets "shows rationale recorded and shows approval recorded" at a time if
    step the step has shown "rationale recorded" at the time
    and step the step has shown "approval recorded" at the time.

when step a step ends
    and step the step was a Deviation
    and it is not the case that step the step meets "shows rationale recorded and shows approval recorded"
then the policy jsf_deviation_record_maintained is broken at step the step.

% jsf_no_dead_code (error): G(¬dead_code)
% JSF++: dead code is executable object code (or data) which, as a result of a design error, cannot be executed and is not traceable to a system or software requirement, and is prohibited.
when step a step ends
    and step the step has shown "dead code"
then the policy jsf_no_dead_code is broken at step the step.

% jsf_runtime_checking_provided (error): G(safety_critical → runtime_checking)
% JSF++ AV Rule 15: provision shall be made for run-time checking (defensive programming); for SEAL 1 or SEAL 2 software, provisions ensure proper operation of software and system function.
when step a step ends
    and step the step has shown "safety critical"
    and it is not the case that step the step has shown "runtime checking"
then the policy jsf_runtime_checking_provided is broken at step the step.

% jsf_shall_deviation_documented (error): G(shall_deviation → documented_in_file)
% JSF++ AV Rule 6: each deviation from a 'shall' rule shall be documented in the file that contains the deviation; deviations from this rule are not allowed.
when step a step ends
    and step the step has shown "shall deviation"
    and it is not the case that step the step has shown "documented in file"
then the policy jsf_shall_deviation_documented is broken at step the step.

% jsf_shall_rules_verified (error): G(GitCommit → P(shall_verified))
% JSF++ §4.2.1: 'shall' rules are mandatory requirements that must be followed and that require verification, either automatic or manual.
step a step meets "an earlier step shows shall verified" at a time if
    step a second step has ended at the time
    and the second step < the step
    and step the second step has shown "shall verified" at the time.

when step a step ends
    and step the step was a GitCommit
    and it is not the case that step the step meets "an earlier step shows shall verified"
then the policy jsf_shall_rules_verified is broken at step the step.

% jsf_shall_violation_deviated (error): G(shall_violation → P(deviation_approved))
% JSF++ §4.2.1: 'shall' rules are mandatory requirements; a violation is permissible only through the formal deviation process.
step a step meets "an earlier step shows deviation approved" at a time if
    step a second step has ended at the time
    and the second step < the step
    and step the second step has shown "deviation approved" at the time.

when step a step ends
    and step the step has shown "shall violation"
    and it is not the case that step the step meets "an earlier step shows deviation approved"
then the policy jsf_shall_violation_deviated is broken at step the step.

% jsf_shall_will_deviation_dual_approved (error): G((shall_deviation ∨ will_deviation) → eng_lead_approved ∧ product_manager_approved)
% JSF++ AV Rule 5: to break a 'will' or a 'shall' rule, approval must be received from both the software engineering lead and the software product manager.
step a step meets "shows shall deviation or shows will deviation" at a time if
    step the step has shown "shall deviation" at the time.

step a step meets "shows shall deviation or shows will deviation" at a time if
    step the step has shown "will deviation" at the time.

step a step meets "shows eng lead approved and shows product manager approved" at a time if
    step the step has shown "eng lead approved" at the time
    and step the step has shown "product manager approved" at the time.

when step a step ends
    and step the step meets "shows shall deviation or shows will deviation"
    and it is not the case that step the step meets "shows eng lead approved and shows product manager approved"
then the policy jsf_shall_will_deviation_dual_approved is broken at step the step.

% jsf_should_deviation_approved (warning): G(should_deviation → eng_lead_approved)
% JSF++ AV Rule 4: to break a 'should' rule, approval must be received from the software engineering lead.
when step a step ends
    and step the step has shown "should deviation"
    and it is not the case that step the step has shown "eng lead approved"
then the policy jsf_should_deviation_approved is broken at step the step.

% jsf_should_violation_recorded (warning): G(should_violation → recorded)
% JSF++ §4.2.1: 'should' rules are advisory; departures are permissible but should be documented.
when step a step ends
    and step the step has shown "should violation"
    and it is not the case that step the step has shown "recorded"
then the policy jsf_should_violation_recorded is broken at step the step.

% jsf_static_analysis_before_commit (error): G(GitCommit → P(StaticAnalysis ∧ jsf_ruleset))
% JSF++ enforcement: rule compliance is established by analysis (and manual review for unverifiable rules) before code is accepted.
step a step meets "an earlier step is a StaticAnalysis and shows jsf ruleset" at a time if
    step a second step has ended at the time
    and the second step < the step
    and step the second step was a StaticAnalysis at the time
    and step the second step has shown "jsf ruleset" at the time.

when step a step ends
    and step the step was a GitCommit
    and it is not the case that step the step meets "an earlier step is a StaticAnalysis and shows jsf ruleset"
then the policy jsf_static_analysis_before_commit is broken at step the step.

% jsf_will_violation_deviated (error): G(will_violation → P(deviation_approved))
% JSF++ §4.2.1: 'will' rules are intended to be mandatory; departures require the formal deviation process (AV Rule 5).
step a step meets "an earlier step shows deviation approved (2)" at a time if
    step a second step has ended at the time
    and the second step < the step
    and step the second step has shown "deviation approved" at the time.

when step a step ends
    and step the step has shown "will violation"
    and it is not the case that step the step meets "an earlier step shows deviation approved (2)"
then the policy jsf_will_violation_deviated is broken at step the step.

scenario governed is:
    % Ponens: every policy of the pack passes on this trace.
    the trace shows "a commit" from 1 to 2.
    step 1 shows "shall verified" from 2 to 3.
    step 1 is a StaticAnalysis from 2 to 3.
    step 1 shows "jsf ruleset" from 2 to 3.
    step 1 ends from 3 to 4.
    step 2 is a Deviation from 4 to 5.
    step 2 shows "rationale recorded" from 4 to 5.
    step 2 shows "approval recorded" from 4 to 5.
    step 2 shows "shall deviation" from 4 to 5.
    step 2 shows "documented in file" from 4 to 5.
    step 2 shows "deviation approved" from 4 to 5.
    step 2 shows "eng lead approved" from 4 to 5.
    step 2 shows "product manager approved" from 4 to 5.
    step 2 shows "recorded" from 4 to 5.
    step 2 ends from 5 to 6.
    step 3 shows "shall violation" from 6 to 7.
    step 3 ends from 7 to 8.
    step 4 shows "will violation" from 8 to 9.
    step 4 ends from 9 to 10.
    step 5 shows "should violation" from 10 to 11.
    step 5 shows "recorded" from 10 to 11.
    step 5 ends from 11 to 12.
    step 6 shows "eng lead approved" from 12 to 13.
    step 6 shows "should deviation" from 12 to 13.
    step 6 ends from 13 to 14.
    step 7 shows "safety critical" from 14 to 15.
    step 7 shows "library use" from 14 to 15.
    step 7 shows "certified library" from 14 to 15.
    step 7 shows "runtime checking" from 14 to 15.
    step 7 ends from 15 to 16.
    step 8 is a GitCommit from 16 to 17.
    step 8 ends from 17 to 18.
    the session ends from 18 to 19.

scenario violating is:
    % Ponens (`ponens trace check --json`):
    %     jsf_certified_libraries_only: failed at step 4
    %     jsf_deviation_record_maintained: failed at step 1
    %     jsf_no_dead_code: failed at step 5
    %     jsf_runtime_checking_provided: failed at step 4
    %     jsf_shall_deviation_documented: failed at step 1
    %     jsf_shall_rules_verified: failed at step 7
    %     jsf_shall_violation_deviated: failed at step 2
    %     jsf_shall_will_deviation_dual_approved: failed at step 1
    %     jsf_should_deviation_approved: failed at step 6
    %     jsf_should_violation_recorded: failed at step 3
    %     jsf_static_analysis_before_commit: failed at step 7
    the trace shows "a commit" from 1 to 2.
    step 1 is a Deviation from 2 to 3.
    step 1 shows "shall deviation" from 2 to 3.
    step 1 shows "eng lead approved" from 2 to 3.
    step 1 ends from 3 to 4.
    step 2 shows "shall violation" from 4 to 5.
    step 2 ends from 5 to 6.
    step 3 shows "should violation" from 6 to 7.
    step 3 ends from 7 to 8.
    step 4 shows "safety critical" from 8 to 9.
    step 4 shows "library use" from 8 to 9.
    step 4 ends from 9 to 10.
    step 5 shows "dead code" from 10 to 11.
    step 5 ends from 11 to 12.
    step 6 shows "should deviation" from 12 to 13.
    step 6 ends from 13 to 14.
    step 7 is a GitCommit from 14 to 15.
    step 7 ends from 15 to 16.
    the session ends from 16 to 17.
